#: ../../source/templates_sanity.md:104
msgid "Principles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_sanity.md:105
msgid ""
"**Extreme negative tracking at scale**: Display headings at 72px+ use "
"aggressive negative letter-spacing (-2.88px to -4.48px), creating a "
"tight, engineered quality that distinguishes Sanity from looser editorial"
" typography."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_sanity.md:106
msgid ""
"**Single font, multiple registers**: waldenburgNormal handles both "
"editorial display and functional UI text. The weight range is narrow "
"(400-425 for most, 500-600 only for tiny labels), keeping the voice "
"consistent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_sanity.md:107
msgid ""
"**OpenType feature control**: Typography uses deliberate feature settings"
" including `\"cv01\", \"cv11\", \"cv12\", \"cv13\", \"ss07\"` for display"
" sizes and `\"calt\" 0` for body text, fine-tuning character alternates "
"for different contexts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_sanity.md:108
msgid ""
"**Tight headings, relaxed body**: Headings use 1.00-1.24 line-height "
"(extremely tight), while body text breathes at 1.50. This contrast "
"creates clear visual hierarchy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_sanity.md:109
msgid ""
"**Uppercase for technical labels**: IBM Plex Mono captions and small "
"labels frequently use `text-transform: uppercase` with tight line-"
"heights, creating a \"system readout\" aesthetic for technical metadata."
msgstr ""

